       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** four doses of 1600 mg is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day, and 1200 mg/day is the usual limit without close supervision.\n- **Risks at that level:** the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day), which is the maximum anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily**, or **400\u2013600 mg PO four times daily**, which are the more typical regimens.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, tell me and note the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
